        "math_academy_id": "q-104927",
        "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)={t}^{2}+3t-2$ onto the subspace spanned by $q(t)=2t-2.$",
        "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9}{\u27e8q(t),q(t)\u27e9}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9 & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,+\\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,+\\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot (2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =16+4 \\\\  & =20,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8q(t),q(t)\u27e9 & =q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,+(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,+(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =16+4+0 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9}{\u27e8q(t),q(t)\u27e9}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{20}\\cdot (2t-2) \\\\  & =2t-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
